---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import OrbStage from '../components/OrbStage.astro';
import { downloads } from '../config/downloads';
---

<Base
  title="Niyora · PMS mood relief that meets you in the moment"
  description="A private iPhone app for the week before your period. Niyora learns when your PMS week is coming, helps you steady in about a minute, and explains why you feel this way. Nothing leaves your phone."
  ogImage="https://assets.niyora.com/niyora-launch-poster.jpg"
  canonicalUrl="https://niyora.com"
>
  <OrbStage />

  <main class="content">
    <section class="hero" data-hue="335" data-sat="58%" data-orb-alpha="0.2" data-orb-scale="0.55">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-text">
          <h1>Make your emotional roller coaster in PMS a breeze.</h1>
          <p class="subhead">The days before your period turn the volume up on everything. Niyora learns when that week is coming, helps you steady in about a minute, and shows you why it's happening.</p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a id="primary-download" href={downloads.appStore} class="app-store-cta">
              <svg class="apple-logo" viewBox="0 0 384 512" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M318.7 268c-.2-36.7 16.4-64.4 50-84.8-18.8-26.9-47.2-41.7-84.7-44.6-35.5-2.8-74.3 20.7-88.5 20.7-15 0-49.4-19.7-76.4-19.7C63.3 141.2 4 184.8 4 273.5q0 39.3 14.4 81.2c12.8 36.7 59 126.7 107.2 125.2 25.2-.6 43-17.9 75.8-17.9 31.8 0 48.3 17.9 76.4 17.9 48.6-.7 90.4-82.5 102.6-119.3-65.2-30.7-61.7-90-61.7-92.6zm-56.6-164.2c27.3-32.4 24.8-61.9 24-72.5-24.1 1.4-52 16.4-67.9 34.9-17.5 19.8-27.8 44.3-25.6 71.9 26.1 2 49.9-11.4 69.5-34.3z"/></svg>
              <span class="ascta-copy"><span class="ascta-top">Download on the</span><span class="ascta-big">App Store</span></span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="trust">
            <div class="trust-row">Free · No account · No wearables · No cycle data shared</div>
            <div class="trust-strong" id="trust-tagline">Your personal details are stripped before anything is sent.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="features" data-hue="330" data-sat="55%">
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3>Reflect</h3>
          <p>Tell Moon what happened. It hands back a few calmer ways to see it, never one verdict to accept.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3>Regulate</h3>
          <p>One small practice to settle your body, done in about a minute. A breath with the orb, cold water, legs up the wall.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3>Respond</h3>
          <p>A clearer way to say what you need. And after a rough moment, a short, honest message ready to send.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="problem" data-hue="300" data-sat="55%">
      <div class="eyebrow">What no one told you</div>
      <h2>Your hormones are normal. Your brain just feels the shift more.</h2>
      <p class="lead">The difference between a hard PMS week and an easy one isn't your hormone levels. It's how strongly your brain responds to the same normal rise and fall. Two in three women feel it as mood swings.</p>
      <div class="research-grid">
        <div class="research-card">
          <h3>Same hormones, different response.</h3>
          <p>When researchers measured them, women who feel awful before their period had the same hormone levels as women who feel fine. The whole difference is sensitivity.</p>
          <div class="cite">NIMH · Schmidt &amp; Rubinow; Hantsoo &amp; Payne, 2020</div>
        </div>
        <div class="research-card">
          <h3>It's wired in, and it runs in families.</h3>
          <p>Premenstrual sensitivity is about 56 percent heritable. The same shift other people barely notice, your system actually feels. A bit like having sensitive skin.</p>
          <div class="cite">Dubey et al, Molecular Psychiatry, 2017</div>
        </div>
        <div class="research-card">
          <h3>It has an end date.</h3>
          <p>When researchers switched these hormones off, the symptoms cleared. When they switched them back on, they returned. It rolls in, and it rolls out, every cycle.</p>
          <div class="cite">NIMH GnRH add-back studies</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="solution" data-hue="278" data-sat="55%">
      <div class="eyebrow">How Niyora helps</div>
      <h2>Reflect. Regulate. Respond.</h2>
      <div class="solution-grid">
        <div class="solution-card">
          <div class="orb-mini orb-pulse"></div>
          <div class="card-eyebrow">Reflect, with Moon</div>
          <h3>A few calmer reads, never a verdict.</h3>
          <p>Tell Moon what happened. Instead of one take to swallow, it offers several steadier ways to see it. Ask for more and it stays gentle. The point is less heat, not the one right answer.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="solution-card">
          <div class="orb-mini orb-breathe"></div>
          <div class="card-eyebrow">Regulate your body</div>
          <h3>About a minute to settle.</h3>
          <p>When you're ready, one small practice brings your body down. Cold water on your face. Legs up the wall. A slow breath with the orb. Short, and made for the moment you're in.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="solution-card">
          <div class="orb-mini orb-rings">
            <span class="ring r1"></span>
            <span class="ring r2"></span>
            <span class="ring r3"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="card-eyebrow">Respond, or repair</div>
          <h3>Say the hard thing better.</h3>
          <p>Then the part that usually goes wrong, made easier. A clearer way to say what you need, or a short, honest message to send after a rough moment. One rough hour isn't the whole story.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="relationships" data-hue="320" data-sat="58%">
      <div class="eyebrow">The people around you</div>
      <h2>PMS strains relationships. It doesn't have to break them.</h2>
      <p class="lead">The week before your period, your reserves run thin and small things land sharp. It isn't that you love anyone less. When you steady yourself first, there's less to spill onto the people you care about.</p>
      <div class="solution-grid">
        <div class="solution-card">
          <div class="card-eyebrow">Name the week</div>
          <h3>One sentence gives them context.</h3>
          <p>"I'm a few days before my period, so I might be more sensitive this week." A sharp moment stops being a mystery.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="solution-card">
          <div class="card-eyebrow">Ask plainly</div>
          <h3>Don't make them guess.</h3>
          <p>"Can you handle dinner." "I need a quiet evening." A plain ask is easier to meet than a mood to read.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="solution-card">
          <div class="card-eyebrow">Repair fast</div>
          <h3>A message, already written.</h3>
          <p>If there's a blowup, Niyora hands you a short, honest apology, ready to send. One rough moment isn't the whole story.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="more-line"><a href="/blog/keeping-your-relationship-healthy-during-pms/">Read: keeping your relationship healthy during PMS →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="248" data-sat="62%">
      <div class="eyebrow">Research backed</div>
      <h2>Every claim has a paper behind it.</h2>
      <p class="lead">No mystic wellness talk. Just findings from peer-reviewed research, cited so you can read the source yourself. And a library of breathing and mindfulness practices, each with the same standard.</p>
      <div class="papers">
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">Differential hormone sensitivity</div>
          <div class="cite">Schmidt et al, NEJM. PMDD brains react to normal hormone levels.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">The heritable trait</div>
          <div class="cite">Dubey et al, 2017. Sensitivity is partly in your genes.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">GABA and the calm brake</div>
          <div class="cite">Allopregnanolone shifts your built-in calm before your period.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">Progressive muscle relaxation for PMS</div>
          <div class="cite">RCT. A large effect on premenstrual symptoms.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">Calcium for PMS</div>
          <div class="cite">Thys-Jacobs crossover RCT. One of the strongest nutrient findings.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">Recognised in 2013</div>
          <div class="cite">Dell'Osso et al, 2024. On average, women waited a decade for a name.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">Box Breathing</div>
          <div class="cite">Used in Navy SEAL training. Lowers cortisol, improves HRV.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">4-7-8 Breath</div>
          <div class="cite">Activates the parasympathetic nervous system. Weil, A.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">5-4-3-2-1 Grounding</div>
          <div class="cite">Linehan, 1993 (DBT). Reduces panic and dissociation.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">Self-Compassion</div>
          <div class="cite">Neff, 2003. Linked to reduced anxiety and rumination.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">Alternate Nostril (Naadishodhana)</div>
          <div class="cite">Sharma et al, 2013. Lowers blood pressure, calms the system.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="paper">
          <div class="title">Ocean Breath (Ujjayi)</div>
          <div class="cite">Pal et al, 2011. Activates the vagus nerve, slows heart rate.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="more-line">and more, every card in Niyora traces back to a source.</p>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="210" data-sat="60%">
      <div class="eyebrow">Private by design</div>
      <h2 id="privacy-tagline">Built to know almost nothing about you.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Your cycle and your feelings are the most personal data there is. Niyora holds as little of it as it can. No account, no profile, no server record of you. Moon's reflections use AI, so we're plain about the one thing that leaves your phone, and what we strip out first.</p>
      <div class="privacy-points">
        <div class="privacy-point">
          <div class="check">✓</div>
          <h3>No account</h3>
          <p>Open the app and start. No sign-up, no login, no profile to fill in.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="privacy-point">
          <div class="check">✓</div>
          <h3>Stripped before it's sent</h3>
          <p>To write Moon's reflections, your words are sent to an AI. First, on your phone, names and other identifying details are removed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="privacy-point">
          <div class="check">✓</div>
          <h3>Cycle data stays yours</h3>
          <p>Your period dates live on your device and drive the app locally. They are never sent off, and never shared.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="founder" data-hue="335" data-sat="60%">
      <div class="eyebrow">Why I built Niyora</div>
      <img src="/neha.jpg" alt="Neha Prasad" class="founder-photo" loading="lazy" />
      <p class="quote">I went looking for a way through PMS that didn't ask me to change my body.</p>
      <p class="quote-body">I'm a doctor, so I started where I trust: the research. And the pattern was hard to miss. Most of what's offered for PMS either medicates it or just tracks it. Very little helps you in the actual hard hour.</p>
      <p class="quote-body">Then I found the quieter, stronger thread. The most reliable, least invasive way through a hard PMS week is emotion regulation. Learning to name what you feel, settle your body, and see the thought from a step back. No hormones to take, no device to wear, no data to hand over.</p>
      <p class="quote-body">That finding is the whole foundation of Niyora. Everything in the app is one small rep of emotion regulation, done in about a minute. I built it for myself first. Now it's yours.</p>
      <div class="signature">Neha Prasad. Doctor, builder, founder of Niyora.</div>
      <div class="founder-cta">
        <a href="/talk" class="cta ghost">Say hello</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="downloads" class="downloads" data-hue="30" data-sat="70%">
      <div class="eyebrow">Get Niyora</div>
      <h2>Start on your iPhone.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Free on the App Store. No account, nothing to set up. Mark your last period and Niyora takes it from there.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a id="downloads-appstore" href={downloads.appStore} class="app-store-cta">
          <svg class="apple-logo" viewBox="0 0 384 512" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M318.7 268c-.2-36.7 16.4-64.4 50-84.8-18.8-26.9-47.2-41.7-84.7-44.6-35.5-2.8-74.3 20.7-88.5 20.7-15 0-49.4-19.7-76.4-19.7C63.3 141.2 4 184.8 4 273.5q0 39.3 14.4 81.2c12.8 36.7 59 126.7 107.2 125.2 25.2-.6 43-17.9 75.8-17.9 31.8 0 48.3 17.9 76.4 17.9 48.6-.7 90.4-82.5 102.6-119.3-65.2-30.7-61.7-90-61.7-92.6zm-56.6-164.2c27.3-32.4 24.8-61.9 24-72.5-24.1 1.4-52 16.4-67.9 34.9-17.5 19.8-27.8 44.3-25.6 71.9 26.1 2 49.9-11.4 69.5-34.3z"/></svg>
          <span class="ascta-copy"><span class="ascta-top">Download on the</span><span class="ascta-big">App Store</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="meta desktop-line">Niyora is also on <a href={downloads.apple} data-arch="apple-silicon">Mac</a> and <a href={downloads.windows} data-arch="windows-x64">Windows</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta" data-hue="30" data-sat="70%">
      <h2>Take the next hard week a little softer.</h2>
      <p class="lead">It takes seconds to install. About a minute to feel different.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a id="final-download" href={downloads.appStore} class="app-store-cta">
          <svg class="apple-logo" viewBox="0 0 384 512" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M318.7 268c-.2-36.7 16.4-64.4 50-84.8-18.8-26.9-47.2-41.7-84.7-44.6-35.5-2.8-74.3 20.7-88.5 20.7-15 0-49.4-19.7-76.4-19.7C63.3 141.2 4 184.8 4 273.5q0 39.3 14.4 81.2c12.8 36.7 59 126.7 107.2 125.2 25.2-.6 43-17.9 75.8-17.9 31.8 0 48.3 17.9 76.4 17.9 48.6-.7 90.4-82.5 102.6-119.3-65.2-30.7-61.7-90-61.7-92.6zm-56.6-164.2c27.3-32.4 24.8-61.9 24-72.5-24.1 1.4-52 16.4-67.9 34.9-17.5 19.8-27.8 44.3-25.6 71.9 26.1 2 49.9-11.4 69.5-34.3z"/></svg>
          <span class="ascta-copy"><span class="ascta-top">Download on the</span><span class="ascta-big">App Store</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="meta">iPhone, iOS 16 or later. Also on Mac and Windows.</div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script is:inline>
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
      var appStoreLocations = {
        'primary-download': 'hero',
        'downloads-appstore': 'downloads_section',
        'final-download': 'final_cta'
      };
      Object.keys(appStoreLocations).forEach(function (id) {
        var el = document.getElementById(id);
        if (!el) return;
        el.addEventListener('click', function () {
          window.posthog?.capture('app_store_clicked', { location: appStoreLocations[id] });
        });
      });

      document.querySelectorAll('a[href*=".dmg"], a[href*=".exe"]').forEach(function (el) {
        el.addEventListener('click', function () {
          window.posthog?.capture('download_clicked', {
            arch: el.dataset.arch || 'unknown',
            location: 'downloads_section',
            version: '0.4.0'
          });
        });
      });

      var sayHello = document.querySelector('.founder-cta a[href="/talk"]');
      if (sayHello) {
        sayHello.addEventListener('click', function () {
          window.posthog?.capture('say_hello_clicked');
        });
      }
    });
  </script>

  <footer>
    <a href="/demo/">Demo</a>
    <a href="/blog/">Writing</a>
    <a href="/changelog/">What's new</a>
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
    <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/neha-prasad-ux/niyora">GitHub</a>
    <a href="mailto:neha@niyora.com">Contact</a>
    <div class="copyright">© 2026 Niyora. Built quietly in Norway.</div>
  </footer>
</Base>

<style>
  .content { position: relative; z-index: 2; }

  section {
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 80px 24px;
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* Compress hero so the feature cards peek into the first viewport,
     signalling there's more page below. */
  .hero {
    min-height: auto;
    padding: 80px 24px 36px;
    max-width: none;
    width: 100%;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .hero { padding: 80px 0 36px; }
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 4px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 50%, 75%, 0.7);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    transition: color 1.4s ease;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 56px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 38px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.3px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  p {
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  p.lead {
    font-size: 20px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }
  p.afterword { margin-top: 36px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; }

  .hero-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .hero-text { width: 100%; }

  .hero .brand {
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45);
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 64px; }
  .hero .subhead {
    font-size: 22px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
    margin: 0 auto 48px;
    max-width: 580px;
  }
  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; }
  .cta {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 16px 36px;
    border-radius: 32px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
    color: rgba(18, 16, 32, 0.95);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
    text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.3px;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease, background 0.3s ease;
    box-shadow:
      0 8px 32px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 55%, 0.35),
      0 0 64px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 60%, 0.2);
  }
  .cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px) scale(1.02);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1);
    color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 70%, 32%, 1);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 2px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 80%, 70%, 0.45),
      0 14px 48px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 80%, 60%, 0.75),
      0 0 100px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 80%, 65%, 0.45);
  }
  .cta.ghost {
    background: transparent;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22);
    box-shadow: none;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
  }
  .cta.ghost:hover { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5); color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); }
  .meta { margin-top: 24px; font-size: 13px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35); }

  /* App Store badge-style button, Apple's dark variant. */
  .app-store-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 12px 22px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: #000;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28);
    color: #fff;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease, border-color 0.3s ease;
    box-shadow:
      0 8px 32px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 55%, 0.28),
      0 0 64px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 60%, 0.15);
  }
  .app-store-cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px) scale(1.02);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 2px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 80%, 70%, 0.35),
      0 14px 48px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 80%, 60%, 0.55),
      0 0 100px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 80%, 65%, 0.35);
  }
  .app-store-cta .apple-logo { width: 26px; height: 26px; flex: none; }
  .ascta-copy { display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 1.05; text-align: left; }
  .ascta-top { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.3px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); }
  .ascta-big { font-size: 21px; font-weight: 500; font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.2px; }

  .trust {
    margin-top: 36px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .trust-row {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
    letter-spacing: 0.3px;
  }
  .trust-strong {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 82%, 0.95);
    letter-spacing: 0.3px;
    transition: color 1.4s ease;
  }

  /* iPhone device mockup rendering the app's pre-session screen. */
  .phone {
    width: 300px;
    max-width: 78vw;
    aspect-ratio: 300 / 620;
    border-radius: 46px;
    padding: 12px;
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, #2a2740, #131120);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    box-shadow:
      0 30px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55),
      0 0 90px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 50%, 0.22);
    transition: box-shadow 1.4s ease;
  }
  .phone-screen {
    position: relative;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 36px;
    background: radial-gradient(120% 90% at 50% 0%, hsla(var(--orb-hue), 45%, 22%, 0.9), #0d0b16 65%);
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
